ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-Youth previously participated in an earlier study by Duflo, Dupas and Kremer in 328 primary schools in the same study site in Western Province, Kenya who consent to\nparticipate.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "raw_text": "-Youth previously participated in an earlier study by Duflo, Dupas and Kremer in 328 primary schools in the same study site in Western Province, Kenya who consent to participate.",\n  "Eq-Comparison": [\n    "previously"\n  ],\n  "Study": [\n    "study"\n  ],\n  "Location": [\n    "Western Province",\n    "Kenya"\n  ],\n  "Eq-Value": [\n    "328"\n  ],\n  "Eq-Operator": [\n    "-"\n  ],\n  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n    "previously"\n  ],\n  "Age": [\n    "Youth"\n  ]\n}<|eot_id|>']
