ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Multipara\n-  Pre-existing cancer (except non-melanoma skin cancer)\n-  Family history of breast cancer (one first-degree female relative diagnosed with breast cancer)\n-  High-risk pregnancy according to national guidelines\n-  During the follow-up, pregnant women under any treatment that may affect the levels of metabolic markers will be excluded from the analysis\n-  Pregnant women with pre-eclampsia or with preterm birth (less than 37 weeks of gestational age) will be also excluded\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "AND": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "- Multipara",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "Multipara"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n                            "Multipara"\n                          ]\n                        },\n                        "right": {\n                          "AND": {\n                            "left": {\n                              "raw_text": "- Pre-existing cancer (except",\n                              "Condition": [\n                                "cancer"\n                              ],\n                              "Eq-Comparison": [\n                                "Pre-existing"\n                              ],\n             