ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Subject who underwent thyroid surgery\n-  Subject who underwent any radiotherapy on neck\n-  Subject who need to neck dissection\n-  Subject under 18 years or over 70 years\n-  Bad general condition\n-  High American Society of Anesthesiologists(ASA) score (over 3)\n-  Breast feeder or pregnancy\n-  Subject who disagree to do this trial\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "AND": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "AND": {\n                            "left": {\n                              "AND": {\n                                "left": {\n                                  "raw_text": "- Subject who underwent thyroid surgery",\n                                  "Procedure": [\n                                    "thyroid surgery"\n                                  ],\n                                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                                    "thyroid surgery"\n                                  ],\n                                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                                    "underwent"\n                                  ],\n                                  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                                    "underwent"\n                                  ]\n                                },\n                                "right": {\n             