ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Non syndromic patients\n-  Medically fit for Surgery\n-  Patient with Primary, complete cleft lip\n-  Patient\'s age younger than six months\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "-"\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "NOT": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "Non syndromic patients",\n                      "Condition": [\n                        "syndromic"\n                      ],\n                      "Negation": [\n                        "Non"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition-Name": [\n                        "syndromic"\n                      ]\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Medically fit for Surgery",\n              "Procedure": [\n                "Surgery"\n              ],\n              "Procedure-Name": [\n                "Surgery"\n              ],\n              "Condition": [\n                "Medically fit"\n              ],\n              "Condition-Name": [\n                "Medically fit"\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "- Patient with Primary, complete cleft lip",\n          "Condition": [\n            "cleft lip"\n          ],\n          "Condition-Name": [\n            "cl