ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Previously documented problems with male reproductive health\n-  Prior diagnosis of male infertility\n-  Use of any prohibited concomitant medication as outlined by protocol\nNote: Other protocol-defined Inclusion/Exclusion criteria may apply.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "raw_text": "- Previously documented problems with male reproductive health",\n          "Condition": [\n            "problems"\n          ],\n          "Condition-Name": [\n            "problems"\n          ],\n          "Observation": [\n            "male reproductive health"\n          ],\n          "Observation-Name": [\n            "male reproductive health"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "Previously"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n            "Previously"\n          ]\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "- Prior diagnosis of male infertility",\n          "Condition": [\n            "male infertility"\n          ],\n          "Condition-Name": [\n            "male infertility"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "Prior"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n            "Prior"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "- Use of any prohibited concomitant medication as outlined by protocol",\n      "Procedure": [\n        "concomitant medication"\n      ],\n      "Procedure-Name": [\n        "concomitant medication"\n      ],\n      "Drug": [\n        "medication"\n      