ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Evidence of clinically relevant pathology\n-  Mental handicap\n-  History of relevant drug and/or food allergies\n-  Regular/routine treatment with non-topical medications within 30 days prior to entry into the clinical research center\n-  Smoking within 60 days prior to drug administration and through the follow-up visit\n-  History of alcohol abuse or drug addiction (including soft drugs like cannabis products)\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "AND": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "- Evidence of clinically relevant pathology",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "pathology"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n                            "pathology"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Operator": [\n                            "-"\n                          ],\n                          "Severity": [\n                            "relevant"\n                          ]\n                        },\n                        "right": {\n                          "raw_text": "- Mental handicap",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "Mental handicap"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n                