ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Volunteers using medication (exception for contraception)\n-  Volunteers having comorbidities\n-  Pregnant women\n-  Women who menstruate on the test date\n-  Volunteers with an implanted elektronical device (IPG, Pacemaker)\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Volunteers using medication (exception for contraception)",\n                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                    "using"\n                  ],\n                  "Drug": [\n                    "medication"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                    "using"\n                  ],\n                  "Exception": [\n                    "exception"\n                  ],\n                  "Drug-Name": [\n                    "contraception"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Volunteers having comorbidities",\n                  "Condition": [\n                    "comorbidities"\n                  ],\n                  "Condition-Name": [\n                    "comorbidities"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Pregnant women",\n              "Condition": [\n                "Pregnant"\n              ],\n              "Condition-Name": [\n                "Pregnant"\n              ],\n              "Life-Stage-And